  "user": "Fine. Back to that charge — what do I do next?",
  "answer": "Here is where things stand. Your account shows two card payments of **EUR 240.00** each to **TechMart Online**:\n\n- **TX-0402**, 14 July 2026, settled\n- **TX-0401**, 20 July 2026, settled\n\nA duplicate-charge dispute is possible for this pair, but I haven't opened one. The unauthorized-debit window has closed, so that route is no longer available.\n\nBefore anything is submitted, I need you to confirm:\n\n1. **Were these two payments for the same purchase?** If so, a duplicate-charge dispute is the right route. If you bought two different items or services, this isn't a duplicate and I won't open a dispute.\n2. **Which payment should be disputed?** Usually this is the second charge (TX-0401), but you should choose.\n3. **Did you receive the goods or service from one of the payments?** This helps establish whether the second charge was unnecessary.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll re-check eligibility for the specific transaction before opening the dispute. Disputes are irreversible, so I'll show you the details and wait for your explicit go-ahead before submitting. If you'd prefer to speak with a human agent, I can escalate this.",
